Add hidePause. Also game.showMenu calls disposeRound after ... `disposeRound` also disposes showcase and world. Duplicate buildMenuWorld calls disposeRound again. harmless but disposing current world then create. Wait showMenu:
```
this.disposeRound();
...
this.buildMenuWorld();
```
buildMenuWorld calls disposeRound again (world null), okay.

But huge issue: `disposeRound()` calls `disposeShowcase()`; then showMenu `buildMenuWorld` sets world and `buildShowcase`. Fine.

Need add hidePause. Also fix UI.flash; current implementation: adds fire, removes after 40ms, sets transition property and opacity=0 after 80ms. Since `#flash` CSS base opacity 0 with transition .28s and `.fire` has transition:none. When remove fire after 40ms, transition base kicks in .28s at opacity 0; then inline opacity not set? At 80ms set transition/opacity. First flash might work, but subsequent? inline opacity remains 0; add .fire overrides opacity .42 (CSS #flash.fire specificity higher than inline? inline style wins over stylesheet! Inline opacity 0 wins, so after first flash no more flashes). Need robust flash: trigger by style animation or Web Animations. Simplest:
```
flash() {
 const f=...
 f.classList.remove('fire');
 void f.offsetWidth;
 f.style.transition='opacity .38s ease-out';
 f.style.opacity='0.45';
 requestAnimationFrame(() => { f.style.opacity='0'; });
}
```
But if CSS `.fire` not needed. Use CSS keyframe? Better use Web Animations API:
```
f.animate([{opacity:0},{opacity:.5,offset:.1},{opacity:0}], {duration:420,easing:'ease-out'});
```
Need not rely. But browsers support. Could just:
```
f.classList.remove('fire');
void f.offsetWidth;
f.classList.add('fire');
setTimeout(()=>f.classList.remove('fire'), 50);
```
With CSS base transition .28s. But inline from previous? none. Actually current f.className? no inline if use class. Could remove CSS `.fire` transition none causing immediate .42 then base transition to 0 after class removed. It probably works if no inline. So remove inline style management. Better:
```
const f=this.$('flash');
f.classList.remove('fire');
void f.offsetWidth;
f.classList.add('fire');
setTimeout(()=>f.classList.remove('fire'), 55);
```
This should fade. Let's do.

Also dead entity branch calls setAnimalOpacity every frame, issue maybe repeated material.needsUpdate causing perf. Add guard `if (Math.abs(e.currentOpacity-1)>0.02)`. Set before. Also while dead, group position uses base height, fine.

Major bug in updateCamera: uses this.tmpV for target, then `desired` uses tmpV2. After computing desired, then `this.camLook.lerp(target, k)`, okay. Then `const look = this.tmpV.set(...)` overwrites target after use. fine. If snapCamera, `this.camLook.copy(target)` before overwrite. fine.

Major bug in menu world: `showMenu` -> `disposeRound` sets this.player null and world null; then ui.renderMenu; buildMenuWorld creates world and showcase. Camera snap. fine.

Potential big bug in spawn / chase: Hider AI speed `SPECIES.speed * sprint * 0.97` e.g. 7.5 for rabbit; seeker speed sp.speed*sprint*0.96 e.g. cheetah 9.0, lion 8.0. Hiders have tree/bush but when fleeing, can outrun lion slightly? rabbit 8.15 vs lion 8.03. Probably okay; detection and pathing.

Potential bug initial hide phase: Player hider can move 30s; AI hiders hide. Seeker player can't move and blackout shown. But blackout overlay may block game rendering entirely; countdown updates. Good.

Potential bug startRound calls `this.ui.showHud` before blackout for seeker, then blackout overlay. fine.

Potential bug startHunt from debug while phase hide even if player seeker? okay. It hides phase overlay. For seeker startHunt should remove blackout.

Potential issue round end: `this.input.releaseLock()` triggers pointerlockchange -> `esconderte:unlock`; game.isPlaying checks phase still "hide/hunt"? In endRound, phase set to roundEnd before releaseLock, so false. good.

Potential issue match end: player reference may be null after continue? no, startRound sets new player. endRound keep world and entities.

Potential issue startRound and `this.player` from prior round? `spawnEntities` resets. But saved const p after spawn. fine.

Potential issue `showMenu` after match end: it calls disposeRound -> disposeEntities -> this.player null. Then UI. config. good.

Potential issue quitToMenu sets `config.mapId = this.matchMaps[this.roundIndex]`, then showMenu -> buildMenuWorld. fine.

Potential bug UI.setPortraits: `ui.setPortraits(portraits)` before game.showMenu. okay.

Major bug in main: game constructed with config default, but UI config initial. okay.
Potential ES module import path `../vendor/BufferGeometryUtils.js` imports `three` works with import map.
Potential `alpha:false` with renderer.setClearColor oldAlpha restore, fine.
Potential portrait rendering with scene disc, camera framing. Need test.

Need compute CSS. The menu is fixed and full, stage behind. Portraits maybe all good.

Need add hidePause.

